Zodiac's change to AngelScript 2.39.0 (altered source, zlib licence term 2; listed in THIRD_PARTY_LICENSES).
Applied by cmake/ZodiacApplyPatch.cmake to the fetched SDK (cmake/Dependencies.cmake), whose files it gives LF line endings first.

Decimal literals compile to the nearest double or float, ties to even, as std::from_chars rounds. AngelScript's own
asStringScanDouble rounded at every digit and again in pow(10.0, exponent) (0.04 came out one ulp off, 5e-324 as zero),
and a float literal was that double rounded once more. A double literal whose double lies exactly halfway between two
floats also carries the float nearest its decimal value, which a conversion of the constant to float uses.

